; Stateful (model-based) property testing, above the core: commands over
; a model, generated programs, and the [stateful] declaration. A suite
; adds windtrap.stateful next to windtrap in its (libraries) and opens
; Windtrap_stateful beside Windtrap. The library consumes the core
; through Windtrap.Private only (the alias block at the top of
; windtrap_stateful.ml is the census) and draws arguments through
; windtrap.gen; no -linkall, because unlike lib/mutation nothing here
; registers itself — linking it does nothing until a suite declares.
;
; Both instrumentation stanzas, matching lib/dune: this module was part
; of the core's measured coverage and mutation population and the move
; must not shrink either set. It runs below the scheduler — a mutant
; here fails reaching tests rather than corrupting the judge — so unlike
; lib/mutation there is no reason to withhold the mutation backend.
; Inert without --instrument-with.

(library
 (name windtrap_stateful)
 (public_name windtrap.stateful)
 (libraries windtrap windtrap_gen)
 (instrumentation
  (backend ppx_windtrap.coverage))
 (instrumentation
  (backend ppx_windtrap.mutate)))
